================================================================================
Third-Party Components
================================================================================

blamepost has zero npm runtime dependencies. It vendors exactly one third-party
component, under lib/vendor/, rather than resolving it from a registry at run
time. The component retains its original copyright and license. Its version, the
registry tarball it came from, and the publisher integrity digest verified before
extraction are all recorded in lib/vendor/MANIFEST.json, alongside a hash of the
extracted tree. The vendored tree is refreshed only through
scripts/vendor-update.sh.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Component:   blamejs
Version:     0.21.8
Package:     @blamejs/core (npm), vendored from the published registry tarball
Source:      https://github.com/blamejs/blamejs
License:     Apache-2.0
Copyright:   Copyright (c) blamejs contributors
Used for:    The entire runtime substrate. Every wire listener composes a
             blamejs mail primitive: b.mail.server.mx (inbound SMTP),
             b.mail.server.submission (authenticated submission),
             b.mail.server.imap, b.mail.server.jmap, b.mail.server.pop3
             and b.mail.server.managesieve, each over the b.mailStore
             message substrate and the b.mail.agent dispatch layer.
             Delivery runs
             through b.mail.send.deliver; inbound authentication through
             b.mail.spf / b.mail.dkim / b.mail.dmarc;
             filtering through b.mail.sieve. Storage, sealed columns, the
             audit chain, the vault, sessions, the HTTP router and the
             security middleware behind webmail and admin all come from the
             same vendored tree (lib/vendor/blamejs/).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

blamejs carries vendored dependencies of its own. They are cryptographic
bundles and data files that are not blamepost's to re-attribute. Their
copyright, license and provenance are recorded in the NOTICE and
lib/vendor/MANIFEST.json that ship inside the vendored tree, at:

    lib/vendor/blamejs/NOTICE
    lib/vendor/blamejs/lib/vendor/MANIFEST.json

Read those files for the full transitive attribution. blamepost does not
restate them here, because restating them creates a second copy that drifts
from the one the code actually loads.
